ing Wolfram language  to to pay attention to the different  parts of humans and Wolfram language and  AI is coming and we're very excited that  we're working in parallel really nicely  with Wolfram and where we're going in  terms of our projects and I thought I'd  conclude with just a few things that  we're really looking forward to  hopefully in 12 points out the first  thing that's really difficult is that so  many people publish everything in PDFs  and in order to get a whole lot of data  together  you have to do something with all the  PDFs the UN lives on PDFs we look  forward to well from having a capacity  to integrate PDF conversion and reading  into that's the one thing where we have  to go outside to Wolfram to do is the  converting of the PDF well we'd love to  never leave Wolfram for our work the  next is that at then we're pretty sure  that this is going to get better but we  find that semantic identification using  text contents using text cases is not  always at the level it's not always  right I guess would be the right way to  put it  sometimes it is sometimes it's not but  we assume the AI is going to get better  on that and consequently identification  will as well and finally we'd like to  see more up to date data in Wolfram  entities we find that sometimes there's  a lag in the Wolfram entities getting  financial data and country data up so I  thank you for your attention we're  looking forward to the future here and  we'll answer any questions if you have  them  [Applause]

